{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1553792-murged-tribes","id":1553792,"title":"Murged Tribes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-12T23:46:56-07:00","id":1553792,"title":"Murged Tribes","content":"So apparently in the BnS version of WtA the Stargazers was forced to join with the Children of Gaia due the damage they took during the apocalypse. Like how the whole thing working maniacally? <br /> (Like are star gazers treated as a large sept within the children, do the children get access to they star gazers gift list, ect) <br /> <br /> And is there any instances of this happening in the mainline WtA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-13T01:16:20-07:00","id":1553794,"title":"","content":"There isn't really any equivalent in the main WtA games (either the old canon, or the W5 one).<br /> <br /> In the pre-W5 canon, the closest examples are Tribes that were so devastated only their kin remained (or at least remained as Gaian) and the kin were taken in by other Tribes with the potential for some of the lost Tribes (specifically the White Howlers and Middle Brother) mystical heritage to crop up in their descendants. There's no real need for mechanical adjustments even if it can be an excuse for allowing some unusual freebies buys.<br /> <br /> There's also the Silver Fangs where Silver Fang Houses have absorbed other Houses that grew to weak over time (ex: Conquering Claw). This has even less mechanical issues because it's just Silver Fangs moving between internal factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-13T04:05:31-07:00","id":1553796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1553792-murged-tribes?p=1553794#post1553794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip.</div> </div> </div> </div>So as far as we the players the star gazer joining the Children of gaia is a totally unprecedented event, since from what I've read about the stargazers made it out of the apocalypse restively intact but still took enough damage that it made long term survival a iffy proposition so they decide to preemptively join up with the ideologically compatible tribe for survival. (apprently they the only tribe with two patron sprites which is wild.)<br /> <br /> Though personally I think simuallr events would have happened at smaller scale (like the Fennia adsorbing smaller celtic tribes as an example). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-13T10:38:39-07:00","id":1553799,"title":"","content":"A more approachable angle might be that the CoGs offer to let some of their cubs and a few more prominent members &quot;retest&quot; under Chimera to patch the holes for this generation and share septs. They can becomes close and possible share some new Camps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-13T20:17:16-07:00","id":1553806,"title":"","content":"I haven't looked at the BNS book since... basically after it came out. IIRC though, the Garou Nation in its take on things was vastly diminished to the point where most Tribes were down to a single Sept because so many Caerns were destroyed. However BNS added the idea of being able to create subsidiary Caerns to build new Septs around even if it would take a long time before they would stop being dependent on the true Caern as a source of connection to the spirit world. So in that version of things, it really could just be that the Stargazers don't have a true Caern of their own and the CoGs are the ones helping them build up what they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-14T18:04:49-07:00","id":1553822,"title":"","content":"The thing is that this is not how tribes work in the canon.<br /> <br /> What defines a tribe is its relationship to spirits, expressed in the forms of the Tribal Totem and the Tribe's Gift List. Everything else is accessory. Above all else, tribes are not defined by their other resources, even if they have an invested interest in them. You can make up for low numbers with kinfolk and/or induction of lost cubs. You can make up for most other resources through multitribal Septs. Tribes like the <b>Siberakh</b> do just fine with extremely limited numbers and resources, and any <b>Siberakh</b> wanting to improve can just join other Septs without giving up their tribal identity, it's just not a thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Middle Brother</b>, the <b>Bunnyip</b> and <b>White Howlers</b> all got Lost because of spirit connections, not physical hardships. One was ritually sacrificed, so the spirits wouldn't recognize the tribe anymore even if their culture, kinfolk and resources were mostly intact. The one who fell to the Wyrm cut ties with spirits in the process (or brought them to the Wyrm). <b>Bunnyip</b> got destroyed because their animal kinfolk went <u><b>completely</b></u> extinct, and that has spiritual ramifications even if their human kinfolk still existed.<br /> <br /> If you still want to make it, what would happen mechanically is that the <b>Stargazers</b> would mostly cease to be. They probably would make a <i>Camp</i> within the <b>Children of Gaia</b>, that would keep some of their Gifts, and a few could be incorporated into the <b>CoG</b> list, but most would be lost. <i>Chimera</i> may become a minor totem or not, but would cease to be a tribal totem as the ex-Gazers embrace <i>Unicorn</i>. Some rituals, Merits and Fetishes of the <b>Stargazers</b> may become available to the <b>Children of Gaia</b>, but some may lose relevance or power because of the tribe not existing anymore.<br /> <br /> Basically that. The main mechanical consequence is one tribe simply not being available anymore and most of their mechanical options being lost. A few may be made available to the other tribe, but this other tribe would be mostly unchanged, or just changed as much as the ST wants, mixing things up a little. Unless you're really wanting to make this unified tribe more powerful than the others, the end result would still be a list of options with mixed elements, but the same size as they were independently.<br /> <br /> From a strategical standpoint it's a loss for everyone, as that reduces the variety of resources available to their Septs. In a version of the setting where the tribes are more independent and fighting for resources more than cooperating on regional Septs, this merge may be a necessity. But under the setting's usual assumptions, nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-23T13:40:02-07:00","id":1553984,"title":"","content":"I was playing with having Croatan, bunyip and howlers as vestigial demographics in relevant tribes. Say 2 dots in pure breed and you get access to some gifts from old tribe totems. <br /> <br /> Howlers-fianna<br /> croatan- the other brothers<br /> bunyip- aborigenee garou in general, im unsure on tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-23T17:10:16-07:00","id":1553987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1553792-murged-tribes?p=1553984#post1553984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was playing with having Croatan, bunyip and howlers as vestigial demographics in relevant tribes. Say 2 dots in pure breed and you get access to some gifts from old tribe totems.<br /> <br /> Howlers-fianna<br /> croatan- the other brothers<br /> bunyip- aborigenee garou in general, im unsure on tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'd use that, I would simplify it to &quot;being from this ethnicity&quot;, or would rather make them a Camp, even if still keeping Pure Breed as a requisite.<br /> <br /> One possible expansion and/or simplification would be for any character with Pure Breed 2 to have the option of access to a few Gifts from another Tribe of the player's choice, representing actual lineage, and for this effect the Lost Tribes are available. Maybe even other Fera, if you want to put in the effort, as we're talking a reduced list instead of access to their full list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-24T00:17:21-07:00","id":1553991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1553792-murged-tribes?p=1553984#post1553984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was playing with having Croatan, bunyip and howlers as vestigial demographics in relevant tribes. Say 2 dots in pure breed and you get access to some gifts from old tribe totems.<br /> <br /> Howlers-fianna<br /> croatan- the other brothers<br /> bunyip- aborigenee garou in general, im unsure on tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remnant White Howler kinfolk were split among the Fianna, Get of Fenris, and Silver Fangs. Remnant Bunyip kinfolk were mostly claimed by Elder Brother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-24T09:11:42-07:00","id":1553994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1553792-murged-tribes?p=1553991#post1553991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remnant White Howler kinfolk were split among the Fianna, Get of Fenris, and Silver Fangs. Remnant Bunyip kinfolk were mostly claimed by Elder Brother.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even despite this traditional splitting, edge cases happen all the time. As no law requires you to be from a given ethnic stock to join any given tribe, exceptions may happen for whatever just 'cause, even if they're not common. Lost Cubs make this particularly common, and miscegenation is a thing, so I would guess a lot of kinfolk and Garou are descendants of <i>any</i> other tribe.<br /> <br /> I think more than trying to figure out where most kinfolk went after those Tribes fell, we should first decide if this &quot;access to Lost Gifts&quot; comes from Spirit pacts or lineage. If it comes from Spirit pacts it's better to ascribe the same number of tribes to each case and run it as a recognition of them as inheritors of the Lost Tribe, regardless of their actual kinfolk. If it comes from lineage, this effect should be available to everyone and give access to every tribe.<br /> <br /> Could even be a new Background, &quot;Lost Kin of (Tribe)&quot;, maybe as an alternative to Pure Breed (as it is effectively Pure Breed for another tribe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-25T00:07:58-07:00","id":1554002,"title":"","content":"There's no need for a clean cut answer to things like access to Gifts. The only mechanical issue is if you're paying in-Tribe or out-of-Tribe costs (or Camp if one goes that route).<br /> <br /> Generally the books present this as an issue of getting the spirits to recognize you as worthy of learning a Gift. Things like existing pacts and lineage are just ways to simplify the process by having the requirements of certain spirits be well known, how to find the right spirits be common knowledge amount the group, and those spirits well inclined to teach them to members of a given group. There are extremely few Gifts in the game where it's impossible to learn them even if you don't have a relevant spirit pact or the right birth (the two books that made the most use of this were Book of Auspices and Rage Across the Heavens). There's a reason why certain secretive Camps are very cautious about revealing their special Gifts: anyone could try to learn them if they know they exist.<br /> <br /> Broadly, to be true to the setting as presented, it's going to be a case-by-case basis. The Incarna Turtle and his direct avatars aren't teaching Middle Brother's best Gifts to anyone, period, though weaker turtle and tortoise spirits are still around that might be able to be convinced to teach Gifts within their purview. The fuzzy areas where character traits, story, and role-playing come in when it comes to things like if you can contact an Ancestor spirit of Middle Brother, and even if you can, can you get information on a Gift considered lost with that Tribe so you can potential earn the right to learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-25T23:39:59-07:00","id":1554018,"title":"","content":"It is a complex yet very intersting and entertainging situation actually<br /> Especially if you play from the frst change, not a full fledged Garou<br /> Generally speking tho' a werewolf have their linieage, Family, Ancestors and &quot;born in a Tirbe&quot; technically they are Garou first and foremost and members of a Tribe second - a Tribe is &quot;just&quot; a very large social unit of the Garou, basically a VERY large Pack bound together with a VERY Strong Totem -, becasue even the characteristics (eg, how the look, behave, etc) and beckground are only secondary, what makes you the member of the Tribe is the fact the Tribe's Totem accepted you<br /> More so, a Garou is not bound to join the tribe of their ancestry; a cub, for example, may not meet the standards expected of a tribe and is therefore unacceptable as a member.<br /> In order to become a full-fledged member of any tribe, ancestral or not, a Garou must pass a Rite of Passage, in which the totem of the tribe accepts them; only then are they viewed as a true tribe member and adult Garou.<br /> <br /> The Rite of Passage is more than a way to prove the Garou's courage, honor and wisdom through harsh trials (potentially and usually by their pack-to-be) alog with other cubs who are also coming of age at the same time<br /> This would-be pack is sent out into the world with a definite goal to achieve, and forbidden to return until it has tried its best to accomplish this goal. Different tribes impose different goals. A Wendigo rite often takes the form of a visionquest, while the Get send their cubs into combat for example.<br /> If the cubs succeed - and usually they are forbidden to return until it has tried its best - to accomplish this goal in their quest, a ritemaster performs this rite upon them, marking them with a pictogram that brands them as full-fledged Garou.<br /> But the point and culmination of a rite is the Tribe's totem accepting and claiming the Cub as her own<br /> ...and the fun part, according the rite and books, while rare it is completely possible more than one Totem Spirit manifest and offers their acceptance<br /> Maybe he had &quot;too much Viking blood&quot;, or too fiercly wyld amazon-like girl, but a would be Shadow Lord cub easly could meet not only Grandfather, who accepts and wants to claim her, but great Fenris and Pegazus also manifest to make their offer (leading very interesting situations, explain bakcground like Enemies and so on)<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, Totems are just spirit and they are like every spirit power hungry and their Tribe is a source of power that more often than not elevated them above the rest, just like how a pack totem becomes stronger<br /> Lion, the Totem of the White Howlers is a very good example. When the Pics succumbed to the Wyrm and the Howlers became Black Spiral Dancers Lion fall from grace, the king of the savannah, the Totem of Respect was forced to become the udnerling of Griffin<br /> He lost considerable power and influence with the fall of his Tribe<br /> But he is not gone<br /> But not on the power level of a Tirbal Totem either, yet<br /> <br /> The Siberakh is a great ewxample, Tribes not only can go extinct, but can appear, and Spirits could be elevated to Tribal level<br /> They are descended from Silver Fangs that saw the folly of inbreeding to maintain their blood purity and instead chose mates from the Wendigo's Stock and Sable, a Totem of Respect, originally member of Falcon's brood took the opportunity<br /> The Tribe (or sub-tribe) is small, yet a Tribe with both Wendigo and Silver Fang ancestors and liniage - arguably the best of two worlds and the Children of Sable are snubbed completely by members of Falcon's brood and cannot communicate with them at all. Falcon not really took well this &quot;rebellion&quot;<br /> But it happened<br /> <br /> of course, Lion Will probably never pull the same stunt, even tho' not all of the Howler's kinfolk became corrupt, and even before the Tribe's fall, intermerriage ( or non consensual unions) between the Fianna and the Fenris and the Holwers have a nice history and the survivors were claimed by those tribes and with the proper breeding, breed, ancestros, pure blood, and tons of other factors a Cub could born with the potential to be a Howler eventually, but it is up to Lion to make the move and claim that one lonely cub in a desperate attempt to rebuild his Tribe<br /> Obviosuly one is... a pretty low number but difference between zero and one is as great as one and infinity<br /> Sable started out as a Pack Totem for those who became eventually the Siberakh (and wisely, her ban is no pack with Sable as their totem may cross the borders of the Siberian region of the former Soviet Union in any direction or for any reason. Sable relies on her children to protect her lands\u2026)<br /> Lion could start again...<br /> Sorry for this little tangent, the point is, in pre WW5 Tribes, Houses do merged\u2026 or went extinct and the survivors absorbed, and in the right condition, they may even return<br /> A Garou\u2026 is a Garou, the Tribe while important is secondary (you can have the best blood, greatest heroes in your family, generations and generations of noble Garou hero who stand behind you\u2026 yet if you managed to born as a male, good luck to be a Black Fury and Pegasus to claim you (unless you are a Metis) and it is up to the Totems if they wants you or not<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-26T04:32:57-07:00","id":1554020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1553792-murged-tribes?p=1554018#post1554018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with the proper breeding, breed, ancestros, pure blood, and tons of other factors a Cub could born with the potential to be a Howler eventually, but it is up to Lion to make the move and claim that one lonely cub in a desperate attempt to rebuild his Tribe</div> </div> </div> </div>This part is completely unnecessary, and mostly easier to do than it seems.<br /> <br /> A lot of people have Pict blood, so this isn't rare to begin with. And it isn't necessarily relevant because this is not exactly the link a spirit looks for, or needs. All other aspects are actually spiritual in nature, even Pure Breed has more to do with being marked by the spirits. Ancestor spirits are spirits, and may choose to approach someone for spirit reasons. What all that means is that Lion can make those things happen, from his perspective they're not a requirement, just a process.<br /> <br /> In fact, Garou that have all those things exist. They appear both among the northern tribes and the BSD and are indistinguishable from what you would expect to be a modern White Howler, except for the fact they're from another tribe.<br /> <br /> What Lion needs to rebuild the tribe is actually two things that can build up each other: enough power to be a Tribal Totem and followers that can build a tribe. In fact, every Lost Tribe can be made anew in this way. From a purely technical standpoint it's easier than it seems, and if this was the goal of their totems they would most likely have returned already, or at least be well in the process.<br /> <br /> Spirits don't do this, though. For whatever reason, most spirits just don't build tribes even when they're powerful enough to do so. This is simply not what they want. We can guess some probable reasons, it seems that becoming a tribal totem is actually a big commitment, something most spirits don't want because their commitment is elsewhere. Tribal totems are extremely important for the Garou, but not exactly all that important to the Umbra compared to other spirits of similar power level. For the totems of the Lost Tribes the events that fell their people extinguished their interest in becoming tribal totems again more than anything, <b>that</b> is why the tribes aren't around anymore.<br /> <br /> Now, the exact details are fuzzy and can be worked in a chronicle by a group wanting to resurrect the Lost Tribes. Lion lost power and seemingly interest in rebuilding the tribe, but it's certainly possible to build up a Lion pack or confederation of packs to the point of recovering his power and will and reignite the White Howlers. You can also go the traditional route of the Last White Howler trope, but that's more of a Garou legend/trope than necessarily the most likely or more interesting avenue to doing so. Turtle, Bunyip and the Rainbow Serpent are all described as in deep slumber out of grief, but that's not necessarily true, what's certain is just that they don't contact Garou anymore. If they're found, they can be convinced to return and build back their tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}